# Text is stored and checked out with LF line ends, whatever core.autocrlf says on this machine. Later lines override
# this one for the files they name.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Shell scripts run in the Linux container straight from the Windows checkout (tools/, docker/), where core.autocrlf would give
# them CRLF line ends and bash would fail on the \r.
*.sh text eol=lf
# cmd misparses batch files with LF-only line ends (it drops characters at line starts).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# The callgrind archives (docs/perf/callgrind, written by tools/profiling/bench.sh): zstd-compressed, never line-ending converted.
*.tar.zst binary
